You can do this by wrapping the input in a relatively-positioned container, then absolutely positioning a **button** (with your SVG) on the right side. The button’s `onClick` can call your function and read the input value.

### React example (recommended)
```jsx
import { useState } from "react";

export default function SearchInput({ onSearch }) {
  const [value, setValue] = useState("");

  const handleClick = () => {
    onSearch(value); // call your function with the current input text
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ position: "relative", width: 320 }}>
      <input
        value={value}
        onChange={(e) => setValue(e.target.value)}
        placeholder="Search..."
        style={{
          width: "100%",
          paddingRight: 44,  // space for the icon button
          height: 40,
          boxSizing: "border-box",
        }}
      />

      <button
        type="button"
        onClick={handleClick}
        aria-label="Search"
        style={{
          position: "absolute",
          right: 8,
          top: "50%",
          transform: "translateY(-50%)",
          width: 32,
          height: 32,
          border: "none",
          background: "transparent",
          cursor: "pointer",
          padding: 0,
        }}
      >
        {/* Your magnifying glass SVG */}
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
          <path
            d="M10.5 3a7.5 7.5 0 105.02 13.06l4.21 4.21 1.41-1.41-4.21-4.21A7.5 7.5 0 0010.5 3z"
            stroke="currentColor"
            strokeWidth="2"
          />
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Usage:
```jsx
<SearchInput onSearch={(text) => console.log("search:", text)} />
```

---

### Plain HTML/CSS/JS version
```html
<div class="search-wrap">
  <input id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." />
  <button id="searchBtn" type="button" aria-label="Search">
    <!-- SVG here -->
    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none">
      <path d="M10.5 3a7.5 7.5 0 105.02 13.06l4.21 4.21 1.41-1.41-4.21-4.21A7.5 7.5 0 0010.5 3z"
        stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
    </svg>
  </button>
</div>

<style>
  .search-wrap { position: relative; width: 320px; }
  .search-wrap input { width: 100%; height: 40px; padding-right: 44px; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .search-wrap button {
    position: absolute; right: 8px; top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 32px; height: 32px;
    border: 0; background: transparent; cursor: pointer; padding: 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.getElementById("searchBtn").onclick = () => {
    const value = document.getElementById("searchInput").value;
    console.log("search:", value);
    // call your function here
  };
</script>
```

